[candidate · 0:51] Let me run it. Two years ago COGS was 42 points of revenue. Beans were 25% of that, so 10.5 points; everything else was 31.5 points. If the non-bean inputs are up 37.5%, that's 31.5 × 1.375 = 43.3 points — an increase of about 11.8 points on its own.

Total COGS rose 16 points, so beans account for the remaining ~4.2 points, going from 10.5 to about 14.7 — roughly a 40% increase, but on a much smaller base.

